IMPORT prelude

-- United Nations Personnel Act 2011 (Singapore) -- who is a UN worker and what is a UN operation (s 3), the offences reaching
-- acts done abroad against UN workers, their premises and vehicles (ss 4, 5, 7), threats (s 6), the presumption of knowledge
-- (s 8), the duty of everyone in Singapore to tell the police (s 9), which foreign offences found extradition (ss 11(9), 12(8)),
-- the Public Prosecutor's consent (s 13), and the First and Second Schedules.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation,
-- version in force from 1/7/2025, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/UNPA2011.txt. The latest amendment annotated
-- is Act 3 of 2021 w.e.f. 01/07/2025 (Schedule items deleted); Act 17 of 2022 w.e.f. 01/07/2022 is annotated on ss 11 and 12.
-- The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is one number out of step with the body; the body's numbers are used.
-- THE SCHEDULE TABLES ARE COLUMN-SHIFTED IN THE .txt DEPOSIT: the descriptions were matched to the section numbers by order of
-- appearance (First Schedule items 5 to 21 and 22 to 31; Second Schedule items 3 to 10), not by line position.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0126 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl), Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance: what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to. No scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to what bears on a person: who is protected, what conduct is caught, the duty to report and its penalty.
-- Not encoded: the Minister's certificate (s 3(5)) beyond a note, mutual legal assistance (s 10), the Gazette-notification
-- machinery of ss 11 and 12 (declared Commonwealth territories, treaties, Orders in Council), the Minister's power to amend the
-- Schedules (s 14), and the punishments of the scheduled offences themselves, which are in other Acts not read here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `United Nations Personnel Act 2011 -- offences`

§§ `3(2) to (4) -- UN operation`

-- s 3(2): a UN operation is one "(a) which is established, in accordance with the Charter ..., by an organ of the United Nations;
-- (b) which is conducted under the authority and control of the United Nations; and (c) which -- (i) has as its purpose the
-- maintenance or restoration of international peace and security; or (ii) has ... been declared by the Security Council or the
-- General Assembly ... to be an operation where there exists an exceptional risk to the safety of the participating personnel."
-- s 3(3): it "also includes" an operation meeting (a) and (b) which is for "(i) delivering humanitarian, political or development
-- assistance in peacebuilding; or (ii) delivering emergency humanitarian assistance."
-- s 3(4): it "does not include any operation -- (a) which is authorised by the Security Council ... as an enforcement action under
-- Chapter VII ...; (b) in which UN workers are engaged as combatants against organised armed forces; AND (c) to which the law of
-- international armed conflict applies." Read literally, the exclusion needs all three; this encoding reads it literally.
DECLARE Operation HAS
    `established by a UN organ under the Charter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under UN authority and control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for international peace and security` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared an exceptional risk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for peacebuilding assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `for emergency humanitarian assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a Chapter VII enforcement action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `UN workers engaged as combatants` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the law of international armed conflict applies` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the operation` IS AN Operation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operation is within s 3(2)` IF
        `the operation`'s `established by a UN organ under the Charter`
    AND `the operation`'s `under UN authority and control`
    AND (   `the operation`'s `for international peace and security`
         OR `the operation`'s `declared an exceptional risk`)

GIVEN `the operation` IS AN Operation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operation is within s 3(3)` IF
        `the operation`'s `established by a UN organ under the Charter`
    AND `the operation`'s `under UN authority and control`
    AND (   `the operation`'s `for peacebuilding assistance`
         OR `the operation`'s `for emergency humanitarian assistance`)

GIVEN `the operation` IS AN Operation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operation is excluded by s 3(4)` IF
        `the operation`'s `a Chapter VII enforcement action`
    AND `the operation`'s `UN workers engaged as combatants`
    AND `the operation`'s `the law of international armed conflict applies`

GIVEN `the operation` IS AN Operation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operation is a UN operation` IF
        (`the operation is within s 3(2)` `the operation` OR `the operation is within s 3(3)` `the operation`)
    AND (NOT `the operation is excluded by s 3(4)` `the operation`)

-- Used by ss 11(9) and 12(8): an offence that is an offence against a UN worker "by virtue only of section 3(3)".
GIVEN `the operation` IS AN Operation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operation counts only by virtue of s 3(3)` IF
        `the operation is a UN operation` `the operation`
    AND (NOT `the operation is within s 3(2)` `the operation`)

§§ `3(1) -- UN worker`

-- s 3(1): a UN worker is a person who is "(a) engaged or deployed by the Secretary-General ... as a member of the military, police
-- or civilian component of a UN operation; (b) in the person's capacity as an official or expert on mission of the United
-- Nations, a specialised agency ... or the International Atomic Energy Agency, present in an area where a UN operation is being
-- conducted; (c) assigned, with the agreement of an organ of the United Nations, by the government of any State or by an
-- intergovernmental organisation to carry out activities in support of the fulfilment of the mandate of a UN operation; (d)
-- engaged by the Secretary-General ..., a specialised agency or the International Atomic Energy Agency to carry out such
-- activities; or (e) deployed by a humanitarian non-governmental organisation or agency under an agreement with the
-- Secretary-General ..., with a specialised agency or with the International Atomic Energy Agency to carry out such activities."
-- s 3(5): a certificate of the Minister for foreign affairs is admissible as evidence of whether a person was a UN worker or an
-- operation a UN operation "until the contrary is proved" (not modelled).
DECLARE Capacity IS ONE OF
    `a member of a military, police or civilian component deployed by the Secretary-General`
    `a UN, specialised agency or IAEA official or expert on mission`
    `assigned by a State or intergovernmental organisation with UN agreement`
    `engaged by the Secretary-General, a specialised agency or the IAEA`
    `deployed by a humanitarian NGO under an agreement with the UN`
    `deployed by a humanitarian NGO with no agreement with the UN`
    `a private contractor of a national government`

GIVEN `the capacity` IS A Capacity, `present in the operation area` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the capacity fits s 3(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the capacity`
    WHEN `a UN, specialised agency or IAEA official or expert on mission` THEN `present in the operation area`
    WHEN `deployed by a humanitarian NGO with no agreement with the UN` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private contractor of a national government` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the capacity` IS A Capacity, `present in the operation area` IS A BOOLEAN, `the operation` IS AN Operation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a UN worker` IF
        `the capacity fits s 3(1)` `the capacity` `present in the operation area`
    AND `the operation is a UN operation` `the operation`

§§ `First and Second Schedules -- the offences that count`

-- First Schedule (offences against UN workers): Corrosive and Explosive Substances and Offensive Weapons Act 1958 ss 3, 4;
-- Hostage-Taking Act 2010 s 3; Kidnapping Act 1961 s 3; Penal Code 1871 ss 302 (murder), 304, 325 (voluntarily causing grievous
-- hurt), 326, 327, 328, 329, 330, 331, 342 (wrongful confinement), 346, 347, 348, 354A ("Outraging modesty in certain
-- circumstances"), 356, 357, 363 (kidnapping), 363A, 364, 365, 366, 367, 368, 375 (rape), 376, 376A. Items 2 and 3 deleted by
-- Act 3 of 2021 w.e.f. 01/07/2025.
-- Second Schedule (offences against premises or vehicles): Penal Code ss 426 (mischief), 427, 435, 436 ("Mischief by fire or
-- explosive substance with intent to destroy a house, etc."), 437, 438, 439, 440. Items 1 and 2 deleted by Act 3 of 2021.
-- Simple hurt, theft and criminal intimidation appear in NEITHER Schedule (their names here are ordinary descriptions; the
-- deposit says nothing about them).
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `murder (Penal Code s 302)`
    `voluntarily causing grievous hurt (Penal Code s 325)`
    `wrongful confinement (Penal Code s 342)`
    `outraging modesty in certain circumstances (Penal Code s 354A)`
    `kidnapping (Penal Code s 363)`
    `rape (Penal Code s 375)`
    `hostage-taking (Hostage-Taking Act 2010 s 3)`
    `possessing a corrosive or explosive substance to cause hurt (CESOWA s 3)`
    `mischief (Penal Code s 426)`
    `mischief by fire or explosive to destroy a house (Penal Code s 436)`
    `simple hurt`
    `theft`
    `criminal intimidation`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is in the First Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `murder (Penal Code s 302)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `voluntarily causing grievous hurt (Penal Code s 325)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `wrongful confinement (Penal Code s 342)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `outraging modesty in certain circumstances (Penal Code s 354A)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `kidnapping (Penal Code s 363)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `rape (Penal Code s 375)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hostage-taking (Hostage-Taking Act 2010 s 3)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `possessing a corrosive or explosive substance to cause hurt (CESOWA s 3)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is in the Second Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `mischief (Penal Code s 426)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `mischief by fire or explosive to destroy a house (Penal Code s 436)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Target IS ONE OF
    `a UN worker`
    `relevant premises or a vehicle used by a UN worker`
    `someone or something else`

GIVEN `the target` IS A Target
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the target is a UN worker` IF
    CONSIDER `the target`
    WHEN `a UN worker` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the target` IS A Target
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the target is UN premises or a UN vehicle` IF
    CONSIDER `the target`
    WHEN `relevant premises or a vehicle used by a UN worker` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `4, 5 and 8 -- acts done outside Singapore`

-- s 4(1): "Any person who commits OUTSIDE Singapore any act -- (a) to or in relation to a person whom he or she knows to be a UN
-- worker; and (b) which, if committed in Singapore, would have constituted an offence specified in the First Schedule, shall be
-- guilty of that offence and ... liable ... to the same punishment"; (2) "may be dealt with as if the offence had been committed
-- in Singapore".
-- s 5(1): the same for an act outside Singapore to premises the person knows to be relevant premises, or a vehicle the person knows
-- is used by a UN worker, "(b) which is likely to endanger the person or liberty of the UN worker", and which would be a Second
-- Schedule offence.
-- s 2(1): "relevant premises" means premises at which a UN worker resides or is staying or which the UN worker uses for the
-- purpose of carrying out his or her functions.
-- s 8(1), (2): once the act to a UN worker (or to relevant premises or a UN worker's vehicle) is proved, "it is presumed, unless the
-- contrary is proved, that the accused knew". Knowledge is therefore modelled as: the accused has NOT proved ignorance.
-- Inference, not text: an act done IN Singapore falls under the scheduled Act itself, so ss 4 and 5 add nothing there.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `the target` IS A Target, `done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the accused proved ignorance of the UN connection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4 makes the act an offence` IF
        `done outside Singapore`
    AND `the target is a UN worker` `the target`
    AND (NOT `the accused proved ignorance of the UN connection`)
    AND `the conduct is in the First Schedule` `the conduct`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `the target` IS A Target, `done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `likely to endanger the UN worker's person or liberty` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused proved ignorance of the UN connection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5 makes the act an offence` IF
        `done outside Singapore`
    AND `the target is UN premises or a UN vehicle` `the target`
    AND `likely to endanger the UN worker's person or liberty`
    AND (NOT `the accused proved ignorance of the UN connection`)
    AND `the conduct is in the Second Schedule` `the conduct`

§§ `6 and 8(3) -- threats`

-- s 6(1): "Any person who, IN OR OUTSIDE Singapore, threatens to commit an act which is -- (a) an offence specified in the First
-- Schedule or under section 4 to or in relation to a person whom he or she knows to be a UN worker; or (b) an offence specified in
-- the Second Schedule or under section 5 to or in relation to [relevant premises or a UN worker's vehicle] ... and which, if
-- committed, is likely to endanger the person or liberty of the UN worker, IN ORDER TO COMPEL any person to do or abstain from
-- doing any act, shall be guilty of an offence". The deposit prints the endangerment words as a second "(b)"; this encoding
-- reads them as part of limb (b) only.
-- Penalty: "a fine or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding -- (c) 7 years; or (d) the term of imprisonment to which a person
-- would be liable for the offence constituted by committing the act threatened ..., whichever is the lesser, or ... both";
-- (2) where no term is prescribed for that offence, 7 years. No cap on the fine is stated.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `the target` IS A Target, `likely to endanger the UN worker's person or liberty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `made to compel someone to act or abstain` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused proved ignorance of the UN connection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the threat is an offence under s 6` IF
        `made to compel someone to act or abstain`
    AND (NOT `the accused proved ignorance of the UN connection`)
    AND (   (`the target is a UN worker` `the target` AND `the conduct is in the First Schedule` `the conduct`)
         OR (    `the target is UN premises or a UN vehicle` `the target`
             AND `the conduct is in the Second Schedule` `the conduct`
             AND `likely to endanger the UN worker's person or liberty`))

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `the threatened offence carries a term of imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN, `its maximum term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for a s 6 threat` MEANS
    IF `the threatened offence carries a term of imprisonment`
    THEN `the lesser of` 7 `its maximum term in years`
    ELSE 7

§§ `7 -- abetment, conspiracy and attempt abroad`

-- s 7: a person who, outside Singapore, commits an act which in Singapore "would constitute an abetment of or a conspiracy or an
-- attempt to commit" a First Schedule or s 4 offence against a known UN worker, or a Second Schedule or s 5 offence against
-- relevant premises or a UN worker's vehicle that "is likely to endanger the person or liberty of the UN worker", "is deemed to
-- commit the act in Singapore". s 8(4) presumes the knowledge.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `the target` IS A Target, `likely to endanger the UN worker's person or liberty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the accused proved ignorance of the UN connection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an abetment, conspiracy or attempt abroad is deemed done in Singapore` IF
        (NOT `the accused proved ignorance of the UN connection`)
    AND (   (`the target is a UN worker` `the target` AND `the conduct is in the First Schedule` `the conduct`)
         OR (    `the target is UN premises or a UN vehicle` `the target`
             AND `the conduct is in the Second Schedule` `the conduct`
             AND `likely to endanger the UN worker's person or liberty`))

§§ `9 -- the duty to tell the police`

-- s 9(1): "Every person in Singapore who has information which the person knows or believes may be of material assistance -- (a) in
-- preventing the commission by another person of a relevant offence; or (b) in securing the apprehension, prosecution or
-- conviction of another person, in Singapore, for an offence involving the commission, preparation or instigation of a relevant
-- offence, and who fails to disclose the information IMMEDIATELY to a police officer shall be guilty of an offence and ... liable
-- ... to a fine not exceeding $50,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 5 years or to both."
-- (2) "No criminal or civil proceedings shall lie against a person for any disclosure made in good faith"; (3) such a person is not
-- "in breach of any restriction upon the disclosure of information imposed by law, contract or rules of professional conduct".
-- (4) "relevant offence" means (a) a First Schedule offence "committed to or in relation to a UN worker"; (b) a Second Schedule
-- offence against relevant premises or a UN worker's vehicle; (c) an offence under s 4 or 5; (d) abetment, conspiracy or attempt.
-- Paragraphs (a) and (b) carry no knowledge requirement, no endangerment requirement and no "outside Singapore" requirement.
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `the target` IS A Target
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a relevant offence under s 9(4)` IF
        (`the target is a UN worker` `the target` AND `the conduct is in the First Schedule` `the conduct`)
    OR  (`the target is UN premises or a UN vehicle` `the target` AND `the conduct is in the Second Schedule` `the conduct`)

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `the target` IS A Target, `the person is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `may help prevent it` IS A BOOLEAN, `may help bring someone to justice in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed immediately to a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to disclose is an offence under s 9` IF
        `the person is in Singapore`
    AND `it is a relevant offence under s 9(4)` `the conduct` `the target`
    AND (`may help prevent it` OR `may help bring someone to justice in Singapore`)
    AND (NOT `disclosed immediately to a police officer`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for failing to disclose` MEANS 50000

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years for failing to disclose` MEANS 5

GIVEN `disclosed in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discloser is shielded from suit and from confidentiality obligations` IF
    `disclosed in good faith`

§§ `11(9) and 12(8) -- which foreign offences found extradition`

-- s 11(9): for a Convention country, "relevant offence" is an offence under its law whose conduct "would constitute an offence
-- against a UN worker, OTHER THAN one which would constitute such an offence by virtue only of section 3(3)".
-- s 12(8): for a "Protocol country" ("a Convention country that is a party to the Protocol"), it is one that "would constitute an
-- offence which is an offence against a UN worker by virtue only of section 3(3)".
-- So an offence against a worker in a peacebuilding or emergency humanitarian operation (s 3(3)) counts only for Protocol
-- countries. Whether the Extradition Act 1968 then applies depends on Gazette notifications and declared Commonwealth territory
-- status, which are not modelled.
GIVEN `the operation` IS AN Operation, `the country is a Convention country` IS A BOOLEAN, `the country is a party to the Protocol` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a relevant offence of that country under s 11 or 12` IF
        `the operation is a UN operation` `the operation`
    AND `the country is a Convention country`
    AND (   (NOT `the operation counts only by virtue of s 3(3)` `the operation`)
         OR `the country is a party to the Protocol`)

§§ `13 -- Public Prosecutor's consent`

-- s 13: "A prosecution under this Act must not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor brings or consents to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution under the Act may be instituted` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor brings or consents to it`
